# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# ROOT CAUSE this file closes (Task 2 fix round 1, 2026-08-08): there was no
# .dockerignore at all, and docker/Dockerfile:18's builder stage runs
# `COPY . .` -- so every file in this directory, including `.env`, entered
# the Docker build context unconditionally. `.gitignore` gives NO protection
# here: it governs git, and Docker never reads it. The build context is the
# repository root (docker/docker-compose.prod.yml:9 sets `context: ..` from
# `docker/`; docs/runbooks/troubleshooting.md:214 runs
# `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` from the repo root) -- which is why
# this file lives here and not under docker/.
#
# This was found, not assumed: a real secret (RESEND_API_KEY in this repo's
# local .env) reached `.next/standalone/.env` via a Turbopack build-tracing
# fallback triggered by lib/framework/bundleHash.ts, and docker/Dockerfile
# copies .next/standalone wholesale into the shipped image. See that file's
# comment and register row D-149 (docs/DEFERRED_REGISTER.md) for the full
# investigation.
#
# TWO-LAYER DEFENSE, both required, neither redundant -- do not delete
# either layer as "covered by the other one":
#   1. THIS FILE stops .env (and the other sensitive/large paths below)
#      entering the build context at all. This is the root-cause fix: the
#      secret is never present in the builder stage in the first place.
#   2. package.json's `postbuild` script (`rm -rf .next/standalone/.env*`)
#      stays as an INDEPENDENT second layer. It exists because the .env leak
#      reached `.next/standalone` through Turbopack's own fallback trace,
#      which is governed by neither .dockerignore nor next.config.ts's
#      outputFileTracingIncludes/-Excludes (verified live, twice). If some
#      future change reintroduces a similar leak by a route this file does
#      not anticipate, the postbuild script is the only thing that catches
#      it, precisely because this file cannot.

# --- Secrets ---
# .env.example is documentation, committed, contains no real values --
# explicitly re-included.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem

# Live session-cookie / credential material -- e2e/fixtures/auth.setup.ts's
# own doc comment: "Playwright storageState files are live session cookies
# for the 20-user fixture ... credential material, not source."
e2e/fixtures/.auth/

# --- Local agent/tooling workspaces ---
# Never source, never a build input. Local tool state that only matters if
# someone ran the given CLI on this workstation and then built from it here
# -- which is exactly why each is listed rather than assumed absent.
# .superpowers/ and .remember/ are already git-ignored (each carries its own
# nested .gitignore) but that has no effect on a Docker build context, which
# is the whole point of this file existing. .remember/ is not named in the
# repo's own .gitignore at all -- found during this investigation by
# checking, not by assuming .gitignore was a complete list; same class of
# risk as .superpowers/, included for the same reason. .vercel IS named in
# .gitignore (Task 2 review, fix round 2, Minor 3, 2026-08-08) and was
# dropped from the first draft of this file with no comment, unlike the
# other two, which were deliberate, reasoned omissions -- this one was not
# reasoned, it was missed; corrected. Inert today (no such directory exists
# in this tree) and only matters if someone runs the Vercel CLI locally and
# then builds from that workstation -- but that is the whole point of an
# exclusion list existing before the day it is needed, not after.
.superpowers/
.remember/
.vercel

# --- Regenerated by the builder stage itself ---
# Copying a host-built copy in first is wasted context-transfer at best
# (node_modules, .next) and a platform-mismatch shadowing risk at worst
# (node_modules' native bindings, app/generated/prisma's compiled query
# engine -- both regenerated in-container by `npm ci` / `npx prisma
# generate`, docker/Dockerfile:17,19).
node_modules
.next
app/generated/prisma
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Legacy/alternate Next.js output paths (mirrors .gitignore) ---
# This project builds with `output: 'standalone'`, not these, but excluding
# is free and matches what git already treats as build output, not source.
out
build

# --- VCS and test artifacts -- never needed by `npm run build` ---
.git
coverage
test-results
playwright-report

# --- OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
